<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The wound UMW_Envenomed's UMW_Stab_Tox leaves UNDER COMBAT EXTENDED. In a vanilla game this
       def is declared and never applied: UMW_Stab_Tox keeps Core's plain Stab injury plus its
       ToxicBuildup additionalHediffs, the ScratchToxic parity its header is built on. Under CE
       the compat root reroutes the DamageDef here and strips the ToxicBuildup
       (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/DamageDefs_CE.xml), and gives this injury CE's
       CombatExtended.HediffCompProperties_Venom with CE's own numbers plus CE's Stab overhaul
       (HediffDefs_CE.xml), so the venom becomes wound-borne exactly as CE makes vanilla's
       ScratchToxic and ToxicBite (its VenomousScratch / VenomousBite, children of Bite) and its
       own VenomousArrow (a child of Cut): the wound feeds CE's VenomBuildup for 10000 to 17500
       ticks at VenomPerSeverity x severity / body size x (1 - ToxicResistance) per tick, tending
       at quality q cuts the rate by (1 - q), permanence stops it, and the injury's own healing
       does not (the rate is fixed when the wound lands). Dose per proc at the trait's amount 3,
       body size 1, untended: 0.40 to 0.70 VenomBuildup (lethal at 1), against the vanilla 0.045
       ToxicBuildup per proc; one tend at quality 0.5 halves it. That is a tenfold dose and
       deliberate: CE's venom is "tend it or die" (one untended CE venomous arrow is lethal on its
       own), and a melee venom outside that model would be the one CE players recognise as not
       CE's. On a mechanoid UMW_Stab_Tox's hediffSolid is Crack, so no venom, as in CE. CE's own
       venomous weapons carry no hunting gate for a wound-borne venom and neither does this.

       WHY THE DEF LIVES IN THE MAIN TREE and not the CE root, which could even inherit CE's
       Name="Stab" (ParentName="Stab" is legal there). The translation checker demands every
       def's injections from the sidecar the L10nProbe dumps on a 1.7 boot, and official CE is
       1.6-only, so a def declared under the CE root can never enter the sidecar and its
       translations can never be validated (1.6/Mods/CLAUDE.md). Declared here, the def is always
       loaded, its strings translate through the normal process, and only its CONSUMER is
       CE-gated. The cost is one unused injury def in a vanilla game, which nothing lists.

       Clone of Core's Stab injury with every number verbatim (vanilla Stab carries no Name=, the
       same gotcha as UMW_Stab_Ragged), so the identity is "a stab wound that carries venom" and
       nothing else: CE's pain and infection overhaul reaches it through the CE-root mirror, the
       same way it reaches the ragged clones. Keep the numbers in step with Stab_Ragged.xml's base
       values if Core's Stab ever changes. The permanent label stays "stab scar": the scar is not
       venomous. -->
  <HediffDef ParentName="InjuryBase">
    <defName>UMW_VenomousStab</defName>
    <label>venomous stab</label>
    <labelNoun>a venomous stab wound</labelNoun>
    <description>A stab wound carrying a slow neurotoxic venom. The venom seeps into the blood until the wound is tended or heals over.</description>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_TendDuration">
        <labelTendedWell>bandaged</labelTendedWell>
        <labelTendedWellInner>sutured</labelTendedWellInner>
        <labelSolidTendedWell>set</labelSolidTendedWell>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Infecter">
        <infectionChance>0.15</infectionChance>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_GetsPermanent">
        <permanentLabel>stab scar</permanentLabel>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <injuryProps>
      <painPerSeverity>0.0125</painPerSeverity>
      <averagePainPerSeverityPermanent>0.00625</averagePainPerSeverityPermanent>
      <bleedRate>0.06</bleedRate>
      <canMerge>false</canMerge>
      <destroyedLabel>Cut off</destroyedLabel>
      <destroyedOutLabel>Cut out</destroyedOutLabel>
    </injuryProps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
